  "slug": "lipid-composition-c3e1",
  "summary": "Seven new works apply coarse-grained models to glycoproteins, filaments, oligomers and lipid-binding sites, extending transferable force fields to new contexts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reduced-resolution simulation used to resolve how proteins assemble and interact with their surroundings. GlycoMarinate automates Martini 3 modelling of N-glycoproteins with transferable and refined glycan models. A shape-based rigid-body model with interface-specific sites simulates PFKL tetramer filament assembly. Multiscale MD with trajectory decomposition maps the aromatic-driven, multivalent self-association of Histatin 1. Coarse-grained MD in POPC links oligomeric interfaces, which reduce membrane defects, to oligomerization type, and CG-MD with SILCS and docking maps cholesterol-binding regions in TRPV6 across open and closed states. Information-theoretic analysis of PrPC simulations and contact-energy clustering of ion channels are analysis methods rather than coarse-grained models. What is new is the breadth of environments, from glycans to membranes, handled by automated or transferable coarse-grained models.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
